# Star Wars: Episode III: Revenge of the Sith (4C410017), Nova. Built from
# the generic survey 1790921690-titleroutes-1082096 (lane.titleroutes
# session 63, reviewed session 64; re-read by lane.titleroutes2 session 1,
# 2026-10-02). Read from its route-frames, not guessed:
#   boot20 (004100): The Collective logo; boot40/booted: the intro movie
#     (FMVs decode with green blocks, #303).
#   cycle 1 (004147 START / 004153 A): "PRESS START" title, then "A long
#     time ago in a galaxy far, far away...".
#   cycles 2-8 (004159-004315): the opening crawl. START and A did not skip
#     it: it ran its full ~80 s.
#   cycles 9-12 (004320-004401): the opening space-battle movie, also not
#     skipped.
#   cycle 13 (004407 START / 004413 A): the end of the movie, then live
#     play: "NEW OBJECTIVE: ESCAPE THE CRUISER HANGAR", Obi-Wan and Anakin
#     with R2-D2, the health HUD.
#   cycle 14 (004419 START / 004425 A): START opens PAUSED (CONTINUE lit)
#     and A continues; the tip "PRESS X AND Y IN DIFFERENT COMBINATIONS TO
#     VARY ATTACKS" is up.
#   play (004451, 004515, 004541): three near-identical frames of Obi-Wan
#     against a wall by a barrel. The survey loop (stick UP, A = jump)
#     walked him into a wall and held him there; the verdict's static
#     window read frozen_frac 0.95. That is the trap this loop avoids.
# So: 15 START/A cycles (13 reached play; the last 2 are a guard against a
# slower boot, and pause + continue if play came on time), mark, then a
# loop with no START that walks four directions in turn (so no one wall
# holds it) and attacks with X and Y. Disk-state risk: the survey left a
# 4C410017 save in the store; if the title offers a Continue/Load menu the
# frames will show which way START/A took it.
# Replay 1 (1790939919-titleroutes2-1446307, ref 282a5af148): no ROUTE FAIL,
# the same path (no Continue menu; play on cycle 13's A, 043818; cycle 14
# pause + continue); the mark (043846) is live play -- the player is
# ANAKIN (HUD portrait), Obi-Wan is the AI partner, beside their wrecked
# starfighter. Then 11 near-identical frames to the end (static_frac
# 0.82): the four legs cancel out, so he never left the spot, and the one
# shot per loop lands at the same point of the loop every time. No enemy
# and no door in any frame. So this version is an EXPLORING loop, not a
# benchmark loop: net movement up (5 s up, 2.5 s right, 2 s left, 1 s
# down per cycle, sliding along whatever wall it meets), X/X/Y combos on
# each leg, and a frame on every leg, so the frames map the hangar and
# show whether droids ever come. Its scored fps carries ~5 screencaps a
# cycle: read it as a route check only.
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
shot booted
repeat 15 {
    press START
    wait 5
    shot menu-start
    press A
    wait 5
    shot menu-a
}
wait 2
shot pre-mark
mark gameplay               # CHECK: the cruiser hangar, the health HUD, no PAUSED panel
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 2.5
    press X
    wait 0.3
    press X
    wait 0.3
    press Y
    wait 0.4
    shot up1
    axis LY mid
    axis LX max
    wait 2.5
    press X
    wait 0.3
    press Y
    wait 0.4
    shot right
    axis LX mid
    axis LY min
    wait 2.5
    press X
    wait 0.3
    press X
    wait 0.3
    press Y
    wait 0.4
    shot up2
    axis LY mid
    axis LX min
    wait 2.0
    press Y
    wait 0.4
    press A
    wait 0.6
    shot left
    axis LX mid
    axis LY max
    wait 1.0
    axis LY mid
    press X
    wait 0.4
    shot back
}
